Hi linux-media,

please find attached a patch that
fixes the build of dtv-scan-tables.
The current release

> https://linuxtv.org/downloads/dtv-scan-tables/dtv-scan-tables-2025-06-06-caca23fb5466.tar.bz2

fails to build due to "unsupported" values in some data files.

Previous bug reports:

> https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2372883#c3
> https://lore.kernel.org/linux-media/1655081924.1.1749464955045@builder.linuxtv.org/
> https://lore.kernel.org/linux-media/CAP4Ef8G8LV+F-Sm7R2RHy0jK29BA1wwt9bVy=asWrSJ5TMM49w@mail.gmail.com/

I can't assess the root cause, but I observed
that certain files cause the problem,
so I created the patch to remove those files.
Since the youngest working release of dtv-scan-tables
is almost two years old, I figured that removing those
files is a sensible temporary solution until corrected
or updated versions of those files become available.

Thanks and best regards -- Yarny

